 "lines": {
  "hook": "Washington has no state income tax on wages.",
  "city": "But does that make its capital affordable? Meet Olympia, where the price of housing might change your mind.",
  "rent": "First, rent. The Census Bureau reports median gross rent of about sixteen hundred dollars a month, based on data from twenty twenty through twenty twenty-four.",
  "buy": "Want to buy instead? The median value of owner-occupied homes was about four hundred eighty-six thousand dollars.",
  "tax": "Now for the twist. Washington has no broad state personal income tax on wages, but that doesn't mean you escape every tax.",
  "transit": "And here's another surprise: local buses operated by Intercity Transit have been fare-free. Check the current service rules before you plan your commute.",
  "summary": "So Olympia offers a state-capital lifestyle, Pacific Northwest scenery, and a transit perk. But housing is the number you really need to watch.",
  "cta": "Would you live in Olympia at these prices? Comment yes or no."
 },
